Package: gitssh
Title: Multi-Account Git, GitHub and SSH Helpers
Version: 0.0.0.9000
Authors@R: 
    person("Wagner", "Faria Barbosa", , "barbosawf@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre"),
           comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0001-8725-2099"))
Description: Helpers to work with Git and GitHub from R when more than one
    account (or more than one machine) is involved. Builds and diagnoses
    multi-account SSH configurations with host aliases, resolves the
    physical home directory when cloud-sync tools redirect user profiles,
    clones, pulls and pushes through the right identity, creates new
    repositories under the right account with guard rails, and wraps
    stash and forced reset/push operations with backups. Cloning and
    pulling public or third-party repositories works without any SSH key.
    Ships a trilingual (Portuguese, English, Spanish) cheat sheet,
    git_tips().
